+## Copy windows
+
+A greedy request whose history (prompt plus output) ends with eight tokens seen
+earlier verifies the tokens that followed their latest earlier occurrence
+instead of dSpark's drafts, up to the draft limit, and dSpark skips its draft
+pass that round (`copy_drafts.rs`; `DS41RT_COPY_DRAFTS=0` disables). Sampled
+requests never copy: in a mixed soak with a third of requests at temperature
+0.7, copied drafts were accepted 52% of the time, against 95% on greedy
+file rewrites. The policy
+does not choose a copy's length: the whole copy is verified, and the lane's
+other requests are selected as usual. A copy is observed without confidence,
+and its round without a prediction, so calibration, per-request outcomes and
+the time bias learn from dSpark drafts only. Its rows and routes still feed the
+layer and round fits and the request's route history. A draft pass beside a
+copy covered fewer requests than the lane, so that round gives no draft-cost
+sample and its draft time is taken out of the round total.
+
 ## Monitoring
 
 `/v1/stats` → `dspark_policy` exports the fitted coefficients and implied
 bandwidth per class and regime, the round fit, prediction error, the draft
 length histogram, acceptance totals, and per-position confidence reliability
 (mean predicted versus observed acceptance where a position was reached).
+Its acceptance totals include copy-window rows, which `copy_drafts` counts
+separately.
 `RUST_LOG=ds41rt::draft_policy=debug` logs each decision and observation.
 
 ## Evaluation against v12
